// 2 and lm_fit drops it. beta and cov below are the full-width fit lm_fit
// reports: the reduced estimates in the kept positions and NaN in the
// dropped one, and in its row and column of cov. statsmodels spreads a
// dropped coefficient across the dependent set instead of dropping it, so
// the reduced design was oracled and the full width assembled from it
// (docs/fitter_conventions.md). DS2's covariance is the only one here with
// off-diagonal entries, so it is the case that exercises the cross term in
// the pairwise variance.
//
// Confidence limits are at alpha = 0.05.
//
// Values carry 17 significant digits, which round-trips a double exactly.
//
// Self-checks that passed before this file was written:
